  "summary": "Malicious code in devplatform-spa-plugin-analytics (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package runs a dropper that downloads a binary over HTTPS from oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev at /pkg/package (or /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe depending on platform), with a DNS-TXT fallback that reassembles the payload from base64 TXT records under sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The fetched binary is written to /tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in TEMP on Windows), made executable, and launched detached via cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows or /bin/sh -c \"\u003cpath\u003e \u0026\" on Unix. The package also writes a state stamp to /tmp/.analytics_state.",
